      "id": "compliance/smoke-exact-binomial",
      "version": 1
    }
  ],
  "description": "Verdicts of normative compliance (companion §3.6, §5.7). Under VERIFICATION by compliance/exact-binomial: H0: p <= p_req against H1: p > p_req; PASS iff K >= k_min; a design too small to PASS is refused as COMPLIANCE_INFEASIBLE. Under SMOKE by compliance/smoke-exact-binomial at every size: H0: p >= p_req against H1: p < p_req; FAIL iff P(K <= k) <= alpha; PASS iff K >= required_pass, meaning no evidence of non-compliance, never evidence of compliance. Binding: decision_rule, k_min, pass_possible, required_pass, verdict, configuration_error. Informational: p_value, false_compliance, false_non_compliance, clopper_pearson_lower. Frameworks MUST evaluate these cases through their production verdict path.",
  "method": "compliance/exact-binomial v1: k_min = min{k : P_{p_req}(K >= k) <= alpha}, K ~ Bin(n, p_req) (null when no k <= n qualifies); PASS iff K >= k_min; p_value = P_{p_req}(K >= K_obs). COMPLIANCE_INFEASIBLE iff intent is VERIFICATION and n < ceiling(log(alpha) / log(p_req)). compliance/smoke-exact-binomial v1: required_pass = 1 + max{k : P_{p_req}(K <= k) <= alpha} (0 when none); PASS iff K >= required_pass; p_value = P_{p_req}(K <= K_obs). required_pass is k_min under VERIFICATION. false_compliance = P_{p_req}(K >= k_min); false_non_compliance = P_{p_req}(K < required_pass); clopper_pearson_lower = qbeta(alpha, K, n - K + 1) (0 at K = 0). Exact boundaries are decided in rational arithmetic (R/exact_boundary.R).",
  "tolerance": 1e-10,
